      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/spoofing",
          "message": {
            "text": "A shared or long-lived bearer token on edge-gateway lets anyone who obtains one copy authenticate as every tenant that uses the same deployment profile. The exposure follows from how edge-gateway receives inbound API requests from auth-broker and hands them to the next stage without an independent check. A successful impersonation exposes every function the genuine caller may use and is hard to tell apart from normal traffic. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Replace the shared bearer token with per-workload identities that rotate automatically, and alert when one identity authenticates from two networks within the rotation window. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for edge-gateway and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "edge-gateway",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Edge DMZ/edge-gateway",
                  "kind": "process"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "41828eafe016e25d",
            "findingId/v1": "S-1",
            "baselineRunId": "2026-09-21T09-12-00"
          },
          "properties": {
            "baselineState": "unchanged",
            "maestro-layer": "L4 \u2014 Deployment Infrastructure",
            "tags": [
              "maestro-layer:L4"
            ],
            "affected_assets": []
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/spoofing",
          "message": {
            "text": "A shared or long-lived refresh token on auth-broker lets anyone who obtains one copy authenticate as every tenant that uses the same deployment profile. Because auth-broker serves the Edge DMZ, a single failure here reaches each consumer of credential assertions and session grants at once. A successful impersonation exposes every function the genuine caller may use and is hard to tell apart from normal traffic. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Replace the shared refresh token with per-workload identities that rotate automatically, and alert when one identity authenticates from two networks within the rotation window. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for auth-broker and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "auth-broker",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Edge DMZ/auth-broker",
                  "kind": "process"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "4cfd16d0f0d8d520",
            "findingId/v1": "S-3",
            "baselineRunId": "2026-09-21T09-12-00"
          },
          "properties": {
            "baselineState": "unchanged",
            "maestro-layer": "L6 \u2014 Security and Compliance",
            "tags": [
              "maestro-layer:L6"
            ],
            "affected_assets": []
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/spoofing",
          "message": {
            "text": "A shared or long-lived tool API key on tool-server-1 lets anyone who obtains one copy authenticate as every tenant that uses the same deployment profile. tool-server-1 runs in the Agent Runtime Zone and exchanges tool call arguments and results with audit-ledger over gRPC over mTLS, so anything able to reach audit-ledger can also reach this weakness. Until the credential is revoked the attacker acts with the victim's authority, and the audit trail attributes the actions to the victim. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Replace the shared tool API key with per-workload identities that rotate automatically, and alert when one identity authenticates from two networks within the rotation window. Verify the control in a pre-production exercise and review it again after any change to tool-server-1."
          },
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "tool-server-1",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Agent Runtime Zone/tool-server-1",
                  "kind": "process"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "a50a80778a188210",
            "findingId/v1": "S-4",
            "baselineRunId": "2026-09-21T09-12-00"
          },
          "properties": {
            "baselineState": "unchanged",
            "maestro-layer": "L3 \u2014 Agent Framework",
            "tags": [
              "maestro-layer:L3",
              "maestro-pattern:trust_exploitation"
            ],
            "affected_assets": []
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/spoofing",
          "message": {
            "text": "An unauthenticated callback or health route on tool-server-1 accepts requests that downstream code treats as if they had come from audit-ledger. audit-ledger trusts tool-server-1 to pass tool call arguments and results along unchanged, which removes the second chance to catch the problem downstream. A successful impersonation exposes every function the genuine caller may use and is hard to tell apart from normal traffic. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Remove implicit trust in route names: authenticate every route of tool-server-1, including callbacks and health checks, and drop requests that carry no verified caller identity. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against tool-server-1, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "tool-server-1",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Agent Runtime Zone/tool-server-1",
                  "kind": "process"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "a50a80778a188210",
            "findingId/v1": "S-5",
            "baselineRunId": ""
          },
          "properties": {
            "baselineState": "new",
            "maestro-layer": "L3 \u2014 Agent Framework",
            "tags": [
              "maestro-layer:L3",
              "maestro-pattern:trust_exploitation"
            ],
            "affected_assets": []
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/tampering",
          "message": {
            "text": "Backups and exports of credential assertions and session grants on auth-broker are writable by operators without a second approver, so a malicious change survives restores. The weakness sits at layer Security and Compliance of the stack, so every workflow that depends on credential assertions and session grants inherits the exposure. Altered data is then treated as authoritative by every consumer, so the damage spreads before anyone compares it with the source. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Protect exports and backups of credential assertions and session grants with write-once storage and dual approval for restore, and verify checksums against a separately held manifest. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to audit-ledger so that responders see them in one place."
          },
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "auth-broker",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Edge DMZ/auth-broker",
                  "kind": "process"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "824bcfd900bb1f02",
            "findingId/v1": "T-1",
            "baselineRunId": "2026-09-21T09-12-00"
          },
          "properties": {
            "baselineState": "unchanged",
            "maestro-layer": "L6 \u2014 Security and Compliance",
            "tags": [
              "maestro-layer:L6"
            ],
            "affected_assets": []
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/tampering",
          "message": {
            "text": "Serialised objects arriving from worker-2 are deserialised by vector-store-a with permissive type handling, allowing crafted payloads to instantiate unintended behaviour. vector-store-a runs in the Data Zone and exchanges embedded documents and metadata with worker-2 over PostgreSQL over TLS, so anything able to reach worker-2 can also reach this weakness. Altered data is then treated as authoritative by every consumer, so the damage spreads before anyone compares it with the source. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Replace permissive deserialisation in vector-store-a with a closed schema of allowed types, and reject payloads that name types outside it. Add a regression test for this abuse path to the CI suite and alert through audit-ledger when the control fires."
          },
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "vector-store-a",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Data Zone/vector-store-a",
                  "kind": "data-store"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "relatedLocations": [
            {
              "id": 0,
              "message": {
                "text": "LLM-6: Anyone who can write to the ingestion path of vector-store-a can slip in documents that contradict..."
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "vector-store-a",
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Data Zone/vector-store-a",
                  "kind": "data-store"
                }
              ]
