          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/tampering",
          "message": {
            "text": "Unsanitised credential assertions and session grants reach auth-broker and are processed as trusted structure, so crafted input changes how later steps interpret the record. The weakness sits at layer Security and Compliance of the stack, so every workflow that depends on credential assertions and session grants inherits the exposure. Altered data is then treated as authoritative by every consumer, so the damage spreads before anyone compares it with the source. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Validate credential assertions and session grants against a strict schema at the boundary of auth-broker, reject unknown fields and normalise encodings before any downstream use. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against auth-broker, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
            {
