          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/repudiation",
          "message": {
            "text": "Clock drift between intake-agent and edge-gateway leaves events in inconsistent order, so the sequence of actions on free-text shipment requests cannot be reconstructed reliably. Because intake-agent serves the Agent Runtime Zone, a single failure here reaches each consumer of free-text shipment requests at once. Without reliable records an investigation cannot establish who acted, so disputes about responsibility stay unresolved. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Synchronise intake-agent and edge-gateway to a trusted time source, record monotonic sequence numbers with every event and alert when drift exceeds one second. Verify the control in a pre-production exercise and review it again after any change to intake-agent."
