          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/repudiation",
          "message": {
            "text": "Operators approve changes to tool call arguments and results through a chat message or ticket comment that is not bound to the executed change, so approvals can be disputed. The weakness sits at layer Agent Framework of the stack, so every workflow that depends on tool call arguments and results inherits the exposure. Incident responders lose the sequence of events, which delays containment and weakens any later accountability claim. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Bind each approval to the exact change hash it covers, record approver and time in the audit ledger and refuse to execute unbound changes. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to audit-ledger so that responders see them in one place."
          },
