        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/information-disclosure",
          "message": {
            "text": "Cross-tenant filters on model-gateway are applied in application code only, so one missing predicate exposes another tenant's prompts and completions. model-gateway runs in the Agent Runtime Zone and exchanges prompts and completions with planner-agent over HTTPS (TLS 1.3), so anything able to reach planner-agent can also reach this weakness. Disclosure is silent, so the affected parties learn about it only when the information is misused. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Enforce tenant isolation in the data layer with row-level policies or separate keys, and add a regression test that queries across tenants. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for model-gateway and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
