        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/denial-of-service",
          "message": {
            "text": "A single oversized or deeply nested payload makes intake-agent spend disproportionate memory and CPU parsing free-text shipment requests. Because intake-agent serves the Agent Runtime Zone, a single failure here reaches each consumer of free-text shipment requests at once. The outage propagates to dependent agents, which stall or retry and prolong the disruption. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Cap payload size, nesting depth and parse time in intake-agent, and reject requests that exceed the limits before allocation. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to audit-ledger so that responders see them in one place."
          },
          "level": "error",
