        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/denial-of-service",
          "message": {
            "text": "Retry storms from worker-2 multiply the load on vector-store-a when it slows down, turning a brief delay into a sustained outage. Because vector-store-a serves the Data Zone, a single failure here reaches each consumer of embedded documents and metadata at once. The outage propagates to dependent agents, which stall or retry and prolong the disruption. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Add jittered exponential backoff and a retry budget to worker-2, and enable a circuit breaker so that vector-store-a can recover. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against vector-store-a, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
