        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/stride/elevation-of-privilege",
          "message": {
            "text": "Object identifiers in requests to edge-gateway are trusted without an ownership check, so a caller can read or change inbound API requests that belong to others. The weakness sits at layer Deployment Infrastructure of the stack, so every workflow that depends on inbound API requests inherits the exposure. Once the boundary is crossed the attacker can reach administrative functions and persist there. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Check ownership or entitlement for every object reference at edge-gateway on the server, and deny by default when the check cannot be made. Add a regression test for this abuse path to the CI suite and alert through audit-ledger when the control fires."
          },
