        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/agentic-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "tool-server-1 retries failed actions on its own, repeating side effects such as bookings or messages when the first attempt partly succeeded. The exposure follows from how tool-server-1 receives tool call arguments and results from worker-2 and hands them to the next stage without an independent check. Actions taken by the agent look legitimate in the logs, which slows detection and complicates rollback. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Make the actions of tool-server-1 idempotent with request keys, cap retries and require confirmation before repeating any action with external effects. Verify the control in a pre-production exercise and review it again after any change to tool-server-1."
          },
          "level": "warning",
