        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/agentic-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "tool-server-1 invokes tools with arguments assembled from model output, so an attacker who shapes the output can call a tool with parameters the designer never allowed. tool-server-1 runs in the Agent Runtime Zone and exchanges tool call arguments and results with audit-ledger over gRPC over mTLS, so anything able to reach audit-ledger can also reach this weakness. The agent acts at machine speed on behalf of the operator, so a single manipulated decision can cause many unwanted changes before a person notices. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Validate every argument against the tool schema in tool-server-1 before the call, enforce allowlists of values and reject free-form commands. Add a regression test for this abuse path to the CI suite and alert through audit-ledger when the control fires."
          },
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
