        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/agentic-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "planner-agent does not limit the rate or total number of tool calls per task, so abuse of a costly tool goes unnoticed until the invoice arrives. planner-agent runs in the Agent Runtime Zone and exchanges task plans and tool selections with model-gateway over HTTPS (TLS 1.3), so anything able to reach model-gateway can also reach this weakness. Actions taken by the agent look legitimate in the logs, which slows detection and complicates rollback. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Apply per-task and per-tool quotas to planner-agent, alert on unusual call patterns and block calls once a cost ceiling is reached. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to audit-ledger so that responders see them in one place."
          },
          "level": "warning",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/security/architecture.md"
                },
                "region": {
