        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/llm-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "Encoded or multilingual payloads bypass the keyword filter in front of intake-agent, which only checks plain English text. Because intake-agent serves the Agent Runtime Zone, a single failure here reaches each consumer of free-text shipment requests at once. The failure is probabilistic, so it may pass pre-release testing and appear only under adversarial input. Rated HIGH likelihood because the path needs no special position and uses interfaces that are exposed by design, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Normalise and decode inputs before filtering in intake-agent, apply semantic checks instead of keyword lists and review filter misses weekly. Name an owner for this control, review it each quarter and route violations to audit-ledger so that responders see them in one place."
          },
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
