        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/llm-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "Encoded or multilingual payloads bypass the keyword filter in front of tool-server-1, which only checks plain English text. audit-ledger trusts tool-server-1 to pass tool call arguments and results along unchanged, which removes the second chance to catch the problem downstream. The failure is probabilistic, so it may pass pre-release testing and appear only under adversarial input. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Normalise and decode inputs before filtering in tool-server-1, apply semantic checks instead of keyword lists and review filter misses weekly. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against tool-server-1, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
