        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/llm-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "intake-agent emits URLs that downstream services fetch, so an attacker can make internal addresses part of the output and trigger server-side requests. edge-gateway trusts intake-agent to pass free-text shipment requests along unchanged, which removes the second chance to catch the problem downstream. The unsafe output reaches an interpreter that trusts it, turning a text generation problem into code or request execution. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Validate URLs from intake-agent against an allowlist, resolve and block private ranges before fetching, and fetch from a restricted network. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for intake-agent and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
