        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/llm-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "intake-agent fabricates reference numbers and clause citations that look real, which operators then paste into official documents. The exposure follows from how intake-agent receives free-text shipment requests from edge-gateway and hands them to the next stage without an independent check. The mistake looks authoritative, so it is rarely questioned until a downstream party objects. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Verify identifiers and citations produced by intake-agent against authoritative systems before display, and mark unverifiable ones clearly. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against intake-agent, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
          "level": "note",
