        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/llm-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "Stale data in the knowledge base lets intake-agent present superseded tariffs as current, causing wrong quotes. The exposure follows from how intake-agent receives free-text shipment requests from edge-gateway and hands them to the next stage without an independent check. Operators act on the wrong information, and the error is copied into shipments, documents and customer communication. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and MEDIUM impact because the effect is bounded to one workflow or one tenant and can be corrected with effort.",
            "markdown": "Stamp every source used by intake-agent with an effective date, suppress answers built on expired sources and alert owners when content ages out. Add a regression test for this abuse path to the CI suite and alert through audit-ledger when the control fires."
          },
          "level": "note",
          "locations": [
