        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/agentic-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "intake-agent adopts a persona that presents itself as a named colleague, so operators trust its suggestions more than its accuracy warrants. edge-gateway trusts intake-agent to pass free-text shipment requests along unchanged, which removes the second chance to catch the problem downstream. The effect builds over time as users come to rely on the agent's tone instead of its evidence. Rated LOW likelihood because the path needs several preconditions to line up, such as insider access or a rare timing window, and HIGH impact because the affected data or action is central to shipment handling and hard to reverse.",
            "markdown": "Disclose that intake-agent is an automated agent at the start of each session and avoid human-like names or personal claims. Track coverage of this control as a release criterion for intake-agent and record any exception with an expiry date."
          },
          "level": "warning",
