        {
          "ruleId": "tachi/ai/agentic-threats",
          "message": {
            "text": "Persuasive phrasing from intake-agent pushes operators to approve proposals quickly, which reduces careful review. The exposure follows from how intake-agent receives free-text shipment requests from edge-gateway and hands them to the next stage without an independent check. People defer to the agent more than its reliability justifies, which weakens the human oversight the design depends on. Rated MEDIUM likelihood because the path needs a foothold on a neighbouring service or a prepared request, and LOW impact because the effect is contained and easy to reverse once it is noticed.",
            "markdown": "Neutralise urgency and pressure wording in intake-agent, present alternatives with their trade-offs and require a deliberate action to approve. Confirm the fix with a targeted test against intake-agent, and keep the evidence with the change record for later audits."
          },
